---
import { cta, demoCta, launchPlan } from '../../lib/site';
---

<!-- The close. It opens the same door the hero opened, in the same words:
     a different label for the same destination re-asks the question the hero
     already answered. The demo is the one quiet alternative for a reader who
     will not start cold, and it is deliberately smaller. The phone number and
     the contact link both live in the footer; repeating them here made the
     last thing on the page a menu instead of an answer. -->
<section id="start" class="border-y border-ticket-rule bg-cream">
	<div class="container-page py-section">
		<div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[7fr_5fr] lg:gap-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl">
				<!-- Eyebrow added 2026-08-26 with the page-wide role register (see
				     src/pages/index.astro). It is the ask, and it is the last of the
				     nine, so it is the one a reader scanning the amber column at speed
				     most needs to find. -->
				<p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
				<h2 class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">Put one real order through it.</h2>
				<p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
					Take a menu and a guest count you already quoted, and see the shopping list, the
					prep sheet, the pack list and the food cost it gives back. Your numbers, not a
					sales demo&rsquo;s.
				</p>

			<!-- The three questions a self-serve trial with a card has to answer before
			     the ask, not after it. Every line below was read off the app on
			     sandbox/demo at c736dbf6 and may not be softened or widened here:
		
			       cancel   -> settings/billing +page.server.ts, the `manage` action calls
			                   auth.api.createBillingPortal. Owner only: ownerBusiness()
			                   throws 403 for any other role. Hence "the owner", not "you".
			       export   -> catalog/recipes/export.csv/+server.ts, whole book, linked in
			                   the recipe list as "Export all recipes". There is NO
			                   ingredient or price-history export, which is why the answer
			                   says so instead of stopping at the good half.
			       day 16   -> same billing page: billing begins at the launch price when
			                   the trial ends unless the owner cancels.
		
			     If any of the three changes in the app, this block moves with it. -->
			<div class="mt-14 border-t border-ticket-rule pt-8">
				<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Before you hand over a card.</h3>
				<dl class="mt-6 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
					<div class="min-w-0">
						<dt class="font-semibold">How do I cancel?</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
							The workspace owner cancels from Settings, then Billing, through Stripe. No
							email to me, no notice period, no talking anyone out of it.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div class="min-w-0">
						<dt class="font-semibold">Can I take my work with me?</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
							The whole recipe book exports as a spreadsheet from the recipe list, any
							time. Ingredient prices do not export yet. That one is on me to build.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div class="min-w-0">
						<dt class="font-semibold">What happens on day sixteen?</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
							Billing starts at {launchPlan.displayPrice} if you did nothing, and nothing
							at all if you cancelled first. There is no invoice for the {launchPlan.trialDays} days.
						</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</div>
			</div>

			<div class="border-t border-ticket-rule pt-6 lg:mt-3">
				<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">What starting costs you</h3>
				<!-- SHORTENED 2026-08-26. The full terms were being told three times on one
				     page: here, in the hero's card disclosure, and again four inches to the
				     left in "What happens on day sixteen?". Three tellings of the same
				     sentence is what makes a page feel like it is talking around the reader.
				     The FAQ beside this one owns the detail now; this line owns the ask. -->
				<p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
					{launchPlan.trialDays} days free. Stripe takes the card, charges $0 today, then
					{' '}{launchPlan.displayPrice} per kitchen workspace unless you cancel. Nothing to install.
				</p>
				<a
					href={cta.href}
					target={cta.target}
					rel={cta.rel}
					aria-label={cta.ariaLabel}
					class="btn-primary mt-7"
				>
					{cta.label}
				</a>
				<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
					Rather watch someone run yours first?{' '}
					<a
						href={demoCta.href}
						target={demoCta.target}
						rel={demoCta.rel}
						aria-label={demoCta.ariaLabel}
						class="btn-quiet">Book 15 minutes</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
